  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "botchan-s04-p0019",
      "source_en": "I thought it was simply a waste of time to talk to such worthless, rotten-spirited fellows. \"Well, if you cannot, or will not, confess what you have actually done, you need not do so, and you may go.\" Thus I dismissed the boys. I am refined neither in speech nor in manner. But I thought I had a good heart—a heart much nobler than that of those cowardly lads. The six boys left me and went on their way placidly and composedly as if they thought they were much superior to their teacher. However, their self-possessed manner itself betrayed their evil disposition. I could never put on such boldness even if I tried.",
